;; repl profile: REPL-only toolset for CLI coding agents (Claude Code, Codex,
;; Gemini CLI). The recommended profile.
;;
;; Current frontier models edit Clojure reliably with the host's own editor, so
;; this profile leaves ALL reading and editing to the host and contributes only
;; what the host lacks: a persistent nREPL connection.
;;
;; Enabled tools:
;;   - clojure_eval      (REPL evaluation, repairs delimiters before evaluating)
;;   - list_nrepl_ports  (discover running nREPL servers, incl. shadow-cljs)
;;   - paren_repair      (safety valve for the rare delimiter tangle)
;;   - cljs_eval, cljs_build_status, cljs_project_state, cljs_list_ns
;;                       (shadow-cljs runtimes; clojure_eval's description
;;                        points ClojureScript work at them)
;;
;; Enabled prompts / resources:
;;   (none)
;;
;; Uses allowlists rather than disable lists, so tools added to clojure-mcp in
;; the future stay off in this profile unless listed here.

{:mcp-instructions
 "A persistent nREPL connection tool is available for evaluating and testing Clojure, ClojureScript, and Babashka code. Use the REPL to explore, verify assumptions, and test changes as you work.

Use your environment's own tools for reading and editing files. A paren_repair tool is available for a delimiter tangle that is hard to fix by string editing."

 :enable-tools [:clojure_eval :list_nrepl_ports :paren_repair
                :cljs_eval :cljs_build_status :cljs_project_state :cljs_list_ns]
 :enable-prompts []
 :enable-resources []

 :write-file-guard false}
